The `Object.defineProperty` is used to define a property (`test`) with a getter and setter. However, in `Object.assign`, you can only assign properties to an object if the object has those properties already. But in this case, `shim` is a **new object** created from `Object.defineProperty`, and you're trying to assign properties to it.

